.TH DIPIFCCRET 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipifccret \- RTP retransmission (RET) and Fast Channel Change (FCC/RAMS) server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipifccret
\fB\-g\fR \fI<cidr>\fR[,\fI<cidr>\fR...]
\fB\-l\fR \fI<addr>\fR:\fI<port>\fR
\fB\-I\fR \fI<iface>\fR
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipifccret
is an RTP retransmission (RET, DVB-IPI Annex F, RFC 4588) and server-based
Fast Channel Change (FCC, DVB-IPI Annex I, built on RFC 6285 RAMS) edge
server. It implements RAMS-based FCC only; Companion Stream FCC (Annex J)
is out of scope for this tool.
.PP
It passively watches a mirrored or SPAN-ported multicast segment through a
raw AF_PACKET capture on the interface given with \fB\-I\fR, rather than
joining channels via IGMP/MLD. A single capture thread feeds per-channel
state for every multicast group inside the \fB\-g\fR range(s); channels are
discovered dynamically as traffic appears, not configured one by one. The
kernel-side capture filter built from \fB\-g\fR always unwraps a single
802.1Q VLAN tag before matching, so a tagged trunk mirror port needs no
extra configuration; only a single VLAN tag is supported (no QinQ).
.PP
For RET, the capture thread keeps a short sequence-keyed ring per channel.
A client NACK on the \fB\-l\fR socket always gets a direct unicast repair
reply, and, when the multicast RET session is enabled, is additionally
repaired over that session (Annex F.5.2). The multicast RET session reuses
the original channel's destination group and port by default (F.6.2.2);
\fB\-F\fR overrides the port, and \fB\-\-no\-mc\-ret\fR disables the session
entirely without affecting the unicast reply path. \fB\-\-no\-rsi\fR turns
off periodic RTCP RSI self-announcement of the \fB\-l\fR target for NACKs.
.PP
For FCC, the capture thread also keeps a Random Access Point (RAP)-anchored
cache per channel. A RAMS-R request arriving just before a channel join is
answered with a burst of the cached data at an accelerated rate
(\fB\-X\fR times the channel's observed nominal bitrate, capped by the
client's requested Max Receive Bitrate if lower), so the receiver can start
decoding immediately instead of waiting for the next RAP in the live
stream. Burst duration is bounded by \fB\-D\fR regardless of signaling, and
a burst is terminated early as congested once
\fB\-\-congestion\-nack\-threshold\fR client NACKs arrive during it.
.PP
RET and FCC can each be disabled independently (\fB\-\-no\-ret\fR,
\fB\-\-no\-fcc\fR), but not both at once. Both protocols share the single
capture thread and the single \fB\-l\fR listen socket, served by \fB\-w\fR
worker threads. Raw packet capture requires the \fBCAP_NET_RAW\fR
capability; either grant it to the binary and run unprivileged, or start
as root and use \fB\-u\fR to drop privileges right after the capture handle
opens.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General options
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-range\ \fI<cidr>\fR[,\fI<cidr>\fR...]
Multicast range(s) to capture, IPv4 or IPv6. Required. Authoritative
whitelist enforced in userspace regardless of the kernel-side filter.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen\ \fI<addr>\fR:\fI<port>\fR
Unicast bind, shared by RET and FCC traffic. Required.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface\ \fI<iface>\fR
Capture interface. Required.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-max\-channels\ \fI<n>\fR
Pre-allocated channel slots. Default: 0 (= 300).
.TP
.B \-\-channel\-idle\-timeout \fI<s>\fR
Free a channel slot after this many seconds with no packets. Default: 120,
0 = never reap.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-rtx\-pt\ \fI<n>\fR
RTP payload type for retransmitted/burst packets. Default: 99.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workers\ \fI<n>\fR
.B \-l
socket worker threads. Default: 0 (= online CPU cores).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-user\ \fI<user>\fR
Drop privileges to this user after opening the capture handle.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Periodic stats on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SS RET (Annex F) options
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ret
Disable RET entirely.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-buffer\ \fI<ms>\fR
Per-channel retransmission buffer depth. Default: 2000.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-ff\-port\ \fI<port>\fR
Multicast RET session port. Default: 0 (= original channel's port).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mc\-ret
Disable the multicast RET session; unicast-only repair.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-ret\-clients \fI<n>\fR
Pre-allocated unicast RTX per-client sequence slots (F.3.2.1). Default:
16384.
.TP
.B \-\-ret\-client\-idle\-timeout \fI<s>\fR
Free a unicast RTX client slot after this many seconds with no NACKs.
Default: 300, 0 = never reap.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-rsi
Disable RSI self-announcement.
.TP
.B \-\-rsi\-interval \fI<s>\fR
RSI self-announcement interval, IPv4
.B \-l
only. Default: 5.
.TP
.B \-\-rsi\-mc\-ret
RSI (F.5.3) rides the MC RET session instead of the default session;
requires MC RET. Matches
.BR dipisds (1)
.BR \-\-ret\-rsi\-mc\-ret .
.TP
.B \-\-rsi\-hostname \fI<name>\fR
Announce this DNS name (SRBT 2) instead of
.BR \-l 's
IPv4 address (SRBT 0) in RSI.
.SS FCC (Annex I) options
.TP
.B \-\-no\-fcc
Disable FCC entirely.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-gop\-cap\ \fI<ms>\fR
Safety cap on cached GOP-in-progress duration. Default: 8000.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-max\-bursts\ \fI<n>\fR
Pre-allocated concurrent burst-session slots. Default: 4096.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-burst\-multiplier\ \fI<n>\fR
Burst rate as a multiple of the channel's observed nominal bitrate.
Default: 1.5.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-burst\-duration\-cap\ \fI<ms>\fR
Hard max burst duration regardless of signaling. Default: 10000.
.TP
.B \-\-max\-buffer\-fill\-bound \fI<ms>\fR
Reject a RAMS-R Min RAMS Buffer Fill Requirement above this (RFC 6285 Sec
10 DoS mitigation). Default: 30000, 0 = no bound.
.TP
.B \-\-fcc\-resolve\-by\-port
Resolve ignore-media-ssrc RAMS-R by a dedicated per-channel port instead
of rejecting with 510. Default: off.
.TP
.B \-\-fcc\-resolve\-base\-port \fI<p>\fR
Base port for
.BR \-\-fcc\-resolve\-by\-port .
Default: 0 (=
.B \-l
port + 1).
.TP
.B \-\-congestion\-nack\-threshold \fI<n>\fR
NACKs during one burst before terminating it as congested (RFC 6285 Sec
6.4). Default: 5, 0 = disabled.
.TP
.B \-\-fcc\-range \fI<cidr>\fR[,...]
Restrict FCC to these
.B \-g
sub-ranges. Default: all of
.BR \-g .
.TP
.B \-\-fcc\-client\-range \fI<cidr>\fR[,...]
Restrict FCC requests to these client source ranges. Default: any client.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipifccret \-g 239.0.0.0/8 \-l 10.0.0.1:6000 \-I eth0
Edge box on a SPAN port mirroring the access switch, RET and FCC both on,
all other settings at their defaults.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
A non-zero status is returned on argument errors or capture/socket
failure. Raw AF_PACKET capture typically requires the
.B CAP_NET_RAW
capability or root privileges; see
.B \-u
above to drop privileges after the capture handle is opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipimetrics (1)
.PP
